# In-Depth Configuration
[% if kind == 'web' %]

## Where configuration comes from

The app reads `config.json` when it starts, at run time, so one image or one `dist/` runs in every environment. Each setting comes from the first of:

1. the deployment's `config.json`, served next to `index.html`[[ ' (mounted over `/usr/share/nginx/html/config.json` in the image)' if container_image else '' ]]
2. the built-in default (`public/config.json` holds the same defaults)

A missing file means the defaults. A value of the wrong type stops the app with an error page that names the setting. nginx serves `config.json` with `Cache-Control: no-cache`, so a changed file reaches the next page load.

